(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["intro-to-pa-profession-pa-intro-master-exam-form-c"]={"title":"Intro to PA Profession Comprehensive Master Exam — Form C","category":"Intro to PA","exam":"General","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"Times of societal turmoil such as war often create a shortage of which professionals, prompting new roles?","choices":["Pharmacists","Nurses","Administrators","Physicians"],"answer":3,"exp":"War and social upheaval have historically produced physician shortages, and it was this kind of turmoil that repeatedly created the opening for new 'physician-substitute' roles like the PA. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Dr. Eugene Stead envisioned a new provider positioned between the level of nurse and:","choices":["Doctor","Administrator","Technician","Pharmacist"],"answer":0,"exp":"Dr. Eugene Stead, the 'father of the profession,' envisioned a new provider positioned between the level of nurse and physician (doctor) who would work closely with, not threaten, physicians. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first PA program was nationally publicized by Reader's Digest and which magazine?","choices":["Life","Newsweek","Look","Time"],"answer":2,"exp":"The first Duke PA program was publicized nationally by both Reader's Digest and Look magazine, helping introduce the new profession to the public. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In the same year the first Duke PA program formed (1965), which two federal programs were created?","choices":["Medicare and Medicaid","FEHB and the VA","ACA and HMO plans","TRICARE and CHIP"],"answer":0,"exp":"1965, the year the first Duke PA program began, was also the year Medicare and Medicaid were created. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which stage of development involves 'acceptance and institutionalization of the profession among health occupations'?","choices":["Maturation","Evaluation","Ideology","Implementation"],"answer":0,"exp":"Maturation is the fifth and final stage of development, marked by acceptance and institutionalization of the profession among health occupations. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Implementation of the PA profession primarily occurred during which period?","choices":["1980-1985","1990-1995","1966-1972","1955-1960"],"answer":2,"exp":"Implementation, the stage where education and regulation frameworks were built, occurred from 1966 to 1972. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Amendments to medical practice acts allowing PA practice were first made in NC, NY, CA, and:","choices":["Washington","Texas","Florida","Colorado"],"answer":3,"exp":"Amendments to medical practice acts allowing PA practice were first made in North Carolina, New York, California, and Colorado. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The 1971 Health Manpower Act provided what for PA programs?","choices":["Accreditation","Certification","State licensure","Federal funding"],"answer":3,"exp":"The 1971 Health Manpower Act provided federal funding for PA programs, supporting the profession's early growth. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first AAPA meeting (1973) was held in Wichita Falls, TX at which location?","choices":["Sheppard Air Force Base","Grady Memorial Hospital","A local VA hospital","Duke University campus"],"answer":0,"exp":"The first AAPA meeting in 1973 was held in Wichita Falls, TX, at Sheppard Air Force Base. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1992, which branches of service began commissioning PAs?","choices":["The Coast Guard branch alone","The Navy branch alone, exclusively","All branches of the armed services","The Army branch alone, exclusively"],"answer":2,"exp":"In 1992, all branches of the armed services began commissioning PAs, expanding the profession's presence in the uniformed services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The 100,000th PA was certified in which year?","choices":["2012","2021","2010","2001"],"answer":0,"exp":"The 100,000th PA was certified in 2012, the same year the PA profession was rated #1 by Forbes/Money. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 2014, NCCPA changed recertification to occur every how many years?","choices":["6","5","10","2"],"answer":2,"exp":"In 2014, NCCPA changed recertification (the PANRE cycle) to occur every 10 years instead of the previous shorter cycle. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The COVID pandemic notably increased PA utilization especially in telemedicine and:","choices":["Radiology work","Pathology work","Mental health","Surgery care"],"answer":2,"exp":"The COVID pandemic notably increased PA utilization especially in telemedicine and mental health services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 2026, how many accredited entry-level PA programs existed?","choices":["222","330","322","476"],"answer":1,"exp":"By 2026, there were 330 accredited entry-level PA programs, reflecting continued growth of the profession. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which of the PAHx core values refers to being the 'primary repository' of the profession's history?","choices":["Dedication","Recognition","Credibility","Engagement"],"answer":2,"exp":"Credibility is the PAHx core value tied to serving as the trusted, primary repository of the profession's history. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Approximately how many accredited PA programs does ARC-PA report?","choices":["476","322","222","330"],"answer":1,"exp":"ARC-PA reports approximately 322 accredited PA programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"ARC-PA accreditation for clinical postgraduate programs is described as a(n):","choices":["Federal requirement","Voluntary process","State requirement","Mandatory process"],"answer":1,"exp":"ARC-PA accreditation of clinical postgraduate programs is a voluntary process (in place since 2019/2020), unlike the mandatory accreditation of entry-level PA programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which standards category do ARC-PA standards address?","choices":["Malpractice rates","Salary benchmarks","Faculty qualifications","Reimbursement schedules"],"answer":2,"exp":"ARC-PA standards address faculty qualifications, along with curriculum, facilities, clinical affiliations, admissions, and fiscal stability. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"PAEA's student section provides information on paying for PA school and the National:","choices":["Institutes of Health","Health Service Corps","Guard","Board of Medical Examiners"],"answer":1,"exp":"PAEA's student section provides information on paying for PA school and the National Health Service Corps. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The NCCPA assures the public that certified PAs maintain the knowledge and cognitive skills to practice:","choices":["Independently only","Safely and effectively","Without supervision","Within any given state"],"answer":1,"exp":"The NCCPA assures the public that certified PAs maintain the knowledge and cognitive skills needed to practice medicine safely and effectively. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which certificate program does NCCPA administer in addition to certification exams?","choices":["PACKRAT","OSCE","CASPA","CAQ"],"answer":3,"exp":"In addition to the certification exams, NCCPA administers the CAQ (Certificate of Added Qualifications) program for PAs practicing in specialty areas. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which is listed as a CAQ offered by NCCPA?","choices":["Anesthesiology","Nephrology","Pathology","Radiology"],"answer":1,"exp":"Nephrology is one of the CAQ specialty areas NCCPA offers, alongside fields like Emergency Medicine, Hospital Medicine, and Psychiatry. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The AAPA vision emphasizes PAs transforming health through patient-centered and what kind of practice?","choices":["Team-based","Independent","Solo","Physician-led"],"answer":0,"exp":"The AAPA vision describes PAs transforming health through patient-centered, team-based practice. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"How many officially recognized specialty organizations are within the AAPA House of Delegates?","choices":["58","22","15","27"],"answer":3,"exp":"There are 27 officially recognized specialty organizations within the AAPA House of Delegates. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The SAAAPA board includes how many regional directors?","choices":["9","6","5","3"],"answer":1,"exp":"The SAAAPA board includes 6 Regional Directors among its leadership positions. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which PAF value is listed alongside 'Making a Difference' and 'Inspiring the Next Generation'?","choices":["Lobbying Congress directly","Nationally Certifying PAs","Accrediting Programs","Supporting Patient Education"],"answer":3,"exp":"Supporting Patient Education is listed among PAF's core activities, alongside 'Making a Difference' and 'Inspiring the Next Generation,' consistent with PAF's mission to improve health through philanthropy and service. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"FAPA holds an annual conference primarily for what purpose?","choices":["Accreditation","Certification testing","CME","Licensure exams"],"answer":2,"exp":"FAPA holds an annual conference primarily for continuing medical education (CME), along with monthly CME dinners. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Student members of FAPA may serve on but generally may not do what with committees?","choices":["Formally vote on chapter business matters","Regularly attend committee meetings","Receive official FAPA publications","Chair them (except Student Affairs)"],"answer":3,"exp":"FAPA student members may serve on committees but generally may not chair them, with the exception of the Student Affairs committee chair, who sits on the board for chapter business. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The PA History Society website is:","choices":["nccpa.net","aapa.org","arc-pa.org","pahx.org"],"answer":3,"exp":"The PA History Society's website is pahx.org. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The Student Academy delegation is the largest in the HOD at how many delegates?","choices":["15","22","13","27"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Student Academy delegation is the largest in the House of Delegates, with 22 delegates. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which PA competency domain covers 'demonstrate a commitment to practicing medicine in ethically and legally appropriate ways'?","choices":["Professionalism and ethics","Interprofessional collaboration","Society and population health","Person-centered care"],"answer":0,"exp":"Professionalism and Ethics is the competency domain that covers demonstrating a commitment to practicing medicine in ethically and legally appropriate ways. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The core competencies were originally developed in response to a growing demand for:","choices":["Accountability and assessment","Fully independent practice","Higher average salaries","Shorter training programs"],"answer":0,"exp":"The core competencies were originally developed in response to a growing demand for accountability and assessment in PA education and practice. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"On PANCE, questions cover 7 knowledge/skill areas and how many disease/disorder categories?","choices":["10","20","7","13"],"answer":3,"exp":"PANCE questions cover 7 knowledge/skill areas and 13 disease/disorder categories. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PANCE is administered at which testing centers?","choices":["Prometric","Pearson VUE","ETS centers","LSAC centers"],"answer":1,"exp":"The PANCE is administered at Pearson VUE testing centers. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"PANCE results are usually available within approximately how long?","choices":["1 month","1 week","2 weeks","24 hours"],"answer":2,"exp":"PANCE results are usually available within approximately 2 weeks of testing. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PANRE recertification exam allots how many hours to complete?","choices":["3 hours","6 hours","5 hours","2 hours"],"answer":2,"exp":"The PANRE recertification exam allots 5 hours to complete. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"During PANRE, reference material availability is:","choices":["Full access allowed","Open-book","Limited formulary only","No reference material"],"answer":3,"exp":"During PANRE, no reference material is available to the test-taker, unlike the longitudinal PANRE-LA option. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"In Florida, PAs are regulated in part by the Medical Practice Act numbered:","choices":["458.347","459.022","456","64B8-30"],"answer":0,"exp":"In Florida, PAs are regulated in part by the (allopathic) Medical Practice Act numbered 458.347. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A Florida temporary PA license expires how long after receipt of exam scores?","choices":["7 days","30 days","1 year","90 days"],"answer":1,"exp":"A Florida temporary PA license expires 30 days after receipt of exam scores. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A Florida temporary PA license may be granted a maximum of how many times?","choices":["Three times","Unlimited","Twice","Once"],"answer":2,"exp":"A Florida temporary PA license may be granted a maximum of two times, with the option to reapply for a one-year extension if the exam was failed. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which body establishes a formulary of medicinal drugs that a Florida PA may NOT prescribe?","choices":["The Florida PA Council","The national AAPA organization","The national NCCPA board","The state FAPA chapter"],"answer":0,"exp":"The Florida PA Council establishes the formulary of medicinal drugs that a Florida PA may not prescribe. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The Professionals Resource Network (PRN) in Florida addresses:","choices":["Formal malpractice claims filed against practitioners","Impairing health conditions/substance misuse","Billing and reimbursement disputes with payers","Initial state licensure applications and renewals"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Professionals Resource Network (PRN) in Florida addresses impairing health conditions and substance misuse among practitioners. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which is TRUE regarding PA billing under Medicaid/TRICARE?","choices":["TRICARE reimburses PAs at 85%; incident-to not permitted","Incident-to billing is always used for TRICARE claims","Medicaid never covers services rendered directly by PAs","TRICARE reimburses PAs at only 50% of the fee"],"answer":0,"exp":"TRICARE reimburses PAs at 85% of the physician fee and does not permit incident-to billing. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Regarding restraint and seclusion, PA orders are time-limited to what range depending on patient age?","choices":["24 hours","6-8 hours","12 hours","1-4 hours"],"answer":3,"exp":"PA orders for restraint and seclusion are time-limited to a range of 1-4 hours, depending on the patient's age. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which is a service PAs are NOT permitted to certify or order?","choices":["Performing a medical screening examination","Certifying terminal illness for hospice","Writing routine prescriptions","Ordering routine laboratory tests"],"answer":1,"exp":"Certifying terminal illness for hospice is a service PAs are not permitted to certify or order — this remains a physician-only certification. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A Patient-Centered Medical Home (PCMH) focuses primarily on:","choices":["Inpatient psychiatry","Acute emergency care services","Primary care coordination","Specialty surgery care"],"answer":2,"exp":"A Patient-Centered Medical Home (PCMH) focuses primarily on primary care coordination, improving outcomes through integrated services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"As of January 2025, Medicare had approximately how many ACOs?","choices":["476","676","176","1,000"],"answer":0,"exp":"As of January 2025, Medicare had approximately 476 Accountable Care Organizations (ACOs), covering over 11 million patients. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Medicare Part B covers which services?","choices":["Prescription drugs","Hospital services","Managed care plans","Outpatient services"],"answer":3,"exp":"Medicare Part B covers outpatient services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Effective interprofessional collaboration requires effective communication enhanced by talking and:","choices":["Actively listening","Supervising staff","Documenting notes","Delegating tasks"],"answer":0,"exp":"Effective interprofessional collaboration requires effective communication, enhanced by both talking and actively listening among the team and patient. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which advanced practice nurse administers anesthesia and earns among the highest nursing salaries?","choices":["CNM","LPN","CRNA","Clinical Nurse Specialist"],"answer":2,"exp":"The CRNA (Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist) administers anesthesia and earns among the highest salaries of any nursing role, around $223K. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A genetic counselor is certified by which board?","choices":["The ARC-PA accreditation commission","ABGC (American Board of Genetic Counseling)","The FSMB physician licensing federation","The NCCPA national certifying board"],"answer":1,"exp":"A genetic counselor is certified by the ABGC (American Board of Genetic Counseling). — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A chiropractor holds which degree?","choices":["Doctor of Physical Therapy","Doctor of Podiatric Medicine","Doctor of Osteopathy","Doctor of Chiropractic"],"answer":3,"exp":"A chiropractor holds a Doctor of Chiropractic degree, earned through a 4-year professional program. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which provider recently gained oral (in addition to topical) medication prescribing privileges in Florida?","choices":["Audiologist","Dietitian","Podiatrist","Optometrist"],"answer":3,"exp":"Optometrists recently gained oral (in addition to topical) medication prescribing privileges in Florida. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A speech-language pathologist requires which degree?","choices":["Master's","Doctorate","Bachelor's","Associate's"],"answer":0,"exp":"A speech-language pathologist requires a Master's degree. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which team member manages resources under 'administration' in patient-centered care?","choices":["Nursing team","Housekeeping","Administration","Maintenance"],"answer":2,"exp":"Administration is the team function that manages resources within patient-centered care, alongside housekeeping (environment), maintenance (comfort/safety), nursing (safety/care), and technicians (diagnostics). — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A podiatrist provides medical and surgical care of the feet, ankles, and:","choices":["Upper limb hands","Lower extremities","Thoracic spine","Shoulder joints"],"answer":1,"exp":"A podiatrist provides medical and surgical care of the feet, ankles, and lower extremities. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Comprehensive care in primary care refers to providing:","choices":["A full range of services","Surgical services","Specialty-only care","Only urgent services"],"answer":0,"exp":"Comprehensive care, one of the '5 C's' of primary care, refers to providing a full range of services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Accessible care means the provider serves as the:","choices":["Consultant role only","First point of contact","Specialist referral","A last-resort option only"],"answer":1,"exp":"Accessible care means the provider serves as the first point of contact for the patient, offering timely access. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"The Joint Commission is best described as a driver of quality improvement and:","choices":["Certification","Licensure status","Patient safety","Reimbursement"],"answer":2,"exp":"The Joint Commission is best described as a driver of quality improvement and patient safety, accrediting healthcare organizations against those standards. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professionalism"},{"q":"Which describes patient-centered care's shift in focus?","choices":["Away from any patient or family input entirely","Toward greater administrative and insurer control","Toward prioritizing insurer cost concerns first","Toward including patient and family perspectives"],"answer":3,"exp":"Patient-centered care reflects a shift toward including patient and family perspectives, moving beyond a purely physician-driven model. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"}]};
